Consider the vector space ${\text{M}}_{2}(\mathbb{R})$ of all $2\times 2$ matrices over $\mathbb{R}.$

Which of the following statements are true?

I. $$
\displaystyle \{\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\ 0 & 0\end{bmatrix},\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\ 0 & 1\end{bmatrix}\}
$$ is a linearly independent set in ${\text{M}}_{2}(\mathbb{R})$

II. $$
\displaystyle \begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\ 0 & 5\end{bmatrix}
$$ can be expressed as a linear combination of $$
\displaystyle \{\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\ 0 & 0\end{bmatrix},\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\ 0 & 1\end{bmatrix}\}
$$

III. $$
\displaystyle \{\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\ 0 & 0\end{bmatrix},\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\ 0 & 1\end{bmatrix}\}
$$ is a basis of ${\text{M}}_{2}(\mathbb{R})$

Given the **orthonormal** basis $$
\displaystyle B=\{\begin{bmatrix}\frac{1}{\sqrt{10}} \\ -\frac{3}{\sqrt{10}}\end{bmatrix},\begin{bmatrix}\frac{3}{\sqrt{10}} \\ \frac{1}{\sqrt{10}}\end{bmatrix}\}
$$ of ${R}^{2},$ find $[x]_{B}$ if $x=\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\ 3\end{bmatrix}.$

Given the **orthonormal** basis $$
\displaystyle B=\{\begin{bmatrix}\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} \\ \frac{1}{2}\end{bmatrix},\begin{bmatrix}\frac{1}{2} \\ -\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}\end{bmatrix}\}
$$ of ${R}^{2},$ find $[x]_{B}$ if $x=\begin{bmatrix}2 \\ -2\end{bmatrix}.$

Given the **orthonormal** basis $$
\displaystyle B=\{\begin{bmatrix}\frac{2}{\sqrt{5}} \\ -\frac{1}{\sqrt{5}}\end{bmatrix},\begin{bmatrix}\frac{1}{\sqrt{5}} \\ \frac{2}{\sqrt{5}}\end{bmatrix}\}
$$ of ${R}^{2},$ find $[x]_{B}$ if $x=\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\ 5\end{bmatrix}.$

Given the **orthonormal** basis $$
\displaystyle B=\{\begin{bmatrix}\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}} \\ -\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\end{bmatrix},\begin{bmatrix}\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}} \\ \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\end{bmatrix}\}
$$ of ${R}^{2},$ find $[x]_{B}$ if $x=\begin{bmatrix}4 \\ 2\end{bmatrix}.$

Given the **orthonormal** basis $$
\displaystyle B=\{\begin{bmatrix}\frac{3}{5} \\ \frac{4}{5}\end{bmatrix},\begin{bmatrix}-\frac{4}{5} \\ \frac{3}{5}\end{bmatrix}\}
$$ of ${R}^{2},$ find $[x]_{B}$ if $x=\begin{bmatrix}-20 \\ 10\end{bmatrix}.$

Given the **orthonormal** basis $$
\displaystyle B=\{\begin{bmatrix}\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}} \\ -\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\end{bmatrix},\begin{bmatrix}\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}} \\ \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\end{bmatrix}\}
$$ of ${R}^{2},$ find $[x]_{B}$ if $x=\begin{bmatrix}2 \\ -4\end{bmatrix}.$

Consider the vector space ${\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\times 2$ matrices over $R.$

Which of the following statements are true?

I. $$
\displaystyle \{\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\ 0 & 0\end{bmatrix},\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\ 0 & -1\end{bmatrix},\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\ 0 & 1\end{bmatrix}\}
$$ is a linearly independent set in ${\text{M}}_{2}(R)$

II. $$
\displaystyle \begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\ 0 & 2\end{bmatrix}
$$ can be expressed as a linear combination of $$
\displaystyle \{\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\ 0 & 0\end{bmatrix},\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\ 0 & -1\end{bmatrix},\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\ 0 & 1\end{bmatrix}\}
$$

III. $$
\displaystyle \{\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\ 0 & 0\end{bmatrix},\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\ 0 & -1\end{bmatrix},\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\ 0 & 1\end{bmatrix}\}
$$ is a basis of ${\text{M}}_{2}(R)$

Consider the vector space ${\text{M}}_{2}(R)$ of all $2\times 2$ matrices over $R.$

Which of the following statements are true?

I. $$
\displaystyle \{\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\ 0 & 1\end{bmatrix},\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\ 0 & 0\end{bmatrix},\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\ 1 & 0\end{bmatrix}\}
$$ is a linearly independent set in ${\text{M}}_{2}(R)$

II. $$
\displaystyle \begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\ 0 & 2\end{bmatrix}
$$ can be expressed as a linear combination of $$
\displaystyle \{\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\ 0 & 1\end{bmatrix},\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\ 0 & 0\end{bmatrix},\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\ 1 & 0\end{bmatrix}\}
$$

III. $$
\displaystyle \{\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\ 0 & 1\end{bmatrix},\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\ 0 & 0\end{bmatrix},\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\ 1 & 0\end{bmatrix}\}
$$ is a basis of ${\text{M}}_{2}(R)$
